<p>macOS kept disabling the accessibility settings of Aerospace, making it close to impossible to start, requiring 8-20 attempts of re-enabling it in the Accessibility settings.</p>
<p>To solve this, I reset the Accessibility database with:</p>
<div class="highlight"><pre><span></span><code>$ tccutil reset Accessibility
</code></pre></div>

<p>The only caveat is that after doing this, you must re-enable all apps
that you want to do special things on your desktop, like OBS studio
and window managers such as Aerospace. Apart from that, it's a safe
operation to do and doesn't require a restart.</p>